82: \begin{abstract}
83: A self-dual five-form in ten dimensions carries a $\dimSelfDualModule$-dimensional
84: space of field values, and the Lorentz-invariant scalar functions built from it
85: organise the possible non-linear self-interactions of the field. We determine
86: the degree-ten sector of this invariant structure exactly.
87: 
88: Working in two independent formulations --- a tensor formulation built from
89: contraction graphs, and a spinor formulation built from chiral bispinors --- we
90: construct an explicit map between them and certify that it is injective with
91: image the gamma-traceless subspace, of rank $\bridgeForwardRank$, with an exact
92: left inverse --- a left inverse, not a two-sided one, since the map is not onto
93: the full symmetric square. The two formulations are then compared degree by
94: degree on common samples, and their spans agree at degrees four, six, eight and
95: ten.
96: 
97: Three results are established exactly over the rationals rather than modulo a
98: prime. The full degree-ten invariant space has dimension $\dimAtenQ$. The
99: subspace reachable by the stress-tensor flow has dimension $\dimDtenQ$, computed
100: by running the closure to its fixed point in exact rational arithmetic after
101: lifting its non-integral targets by rational reconstruction. The quotient of the
102: first by the second therefore has dimension $\dimQtenQ$: there are three
103: independent degree-ten invariant directions that this flow does not reach. We
104: also show that the span of the previously published degree-ten structures meets
105: the product sector in exactly one dimension, and we write that intersection out

