20: \date{\today}
21: 
22: \begin{abstract}
23: Non-linear theories of a chiral four-form gauge field in ten dimensions are
24: usually constructed by deforming a seed theory along a flow built from
25: stress-tensor invariants, as in lower dimensions where such flows generate
26: everything available. Whether that construction reaches the whole space of local
27: interactions in ten dimensions has not been decidable, because the space itself
28: was not known at any fixed order. We determine it exactly at quartic-squared
29: order: the space of local invariants of degree ten in the self-dual five-form is
30: \dimAten-dimensional, the subspace reachable by the stress-tensor flow is
31: \dimDten-dimensional, and the quotient is exactly \dimQten-dimensional. We give
32: explicit representatives of the three unreachable directions, no proper subset of
33: which spans the quotient. Products of lower-degree invariants are all reachable, so the missing
34: directions are not built from anything simpler. The result is obtained in exact
35: arithmetic and recovered independently in graph, block-tensor and spinor
36: descriptions related by a certified equivariant map. Any deformation scheme
37: intended to cover ten-dimensional chiral four-form dynamics at this order must
38: therefore enlarge its generator set by at least three independent structures.
39: \end{abstract}
