55: \begin{abstract}
56: The Lorentz-invariant scalar functions of a self-dual five-form in ten
57: dimensions control the non-linear self-interactions the field can have. We
58: determine the degree-ten sector of this structure exactly over $\Q$, rather than
59: modulo a prime. The full invariant space has dimension $\dimAtenQ$; the subspace
60: activated by the stress-tensor flow has dimension $\dimDtenQ$; the quotient
61: therefore has dimension $\dimQtenQ$, so three independent degree-ten directions
62: lie outside the reach of the flow. The separation rests on a short theorem: the
63: free stress tensor of a self-dual five-form is traceless for every improvement
64: coefficient, because $F\wedge F$ vanishes identically for a form of odd degree,
65: so $\operatorname{Tr}\tau$ begins at field degree four rather than two. Forcing
66: the naive degree-two start collapses the quotient to zero. We certify a
67: tensor--spinor bridge of rank $\bridgeForwardRank$ with an exact left inverse,
68: certify generic functional rank at least $\charZeroLowerBound$ by an explicit
69: $\minorSize\times\minorSize$ integer minor, and give the one-dimensional overlap
70: between the published degree-ten span and the product sector as an exact integer
71: identity. All computations are exact; none uses floating point.
72: \end{abstract}
